  "_pathology_normalisation": {
    "reason": "The pathology order parameter is EXTENSIVE: it scales with sum(outer(core,core)), which is 4.0 for the 2-bead Abeta42 core and 207.4 for the 16-bead polyQ36 core. Inheriting Abeta42's coefficients put HTT permanently above path_thresh, saturating damage and leaving no headroom for intervention.",
    "scale_factor": 0.019286403085824494,
    "derivation": "core-pair mass ratio, measured; not fitted to the gate outcome",
    "note": "Per-task profile values only. The frozen environment code, policy schema, verifier and reward form are unchanged."
  },
  "_extensive_parameter_normalisation": {
    "problem": "Several profile parameters are EXTENSIVE - their natural scale grows with system size - so inheriting them from a smaller protein silently saturates the damage channel and masks every downstream gate.",
    "normalised": {
      "path_inter/intra/nucleus/locked": "x0.019286 (core-pair mass ratio 4.0/207.4)",
      "safe_pathology": "1.8 -> 0.034716 (same path scale)",
      "elastic_limit": "42.57 = p90 of the no-op E_bond+E_angle distribution under the current chemistry. Rule: charge irreversible damage only for geometry beyond the 90th percentile of the UNCONTROLLED working range. This reproduces the original Abeta42 value (20.0 vs p90 20.13); the '1.418x median' multiple used earlier was a post-hoc description, not the rule.",
      "eta_disrupt": "0.12 -> 0.065217 (protective-pair mass ratio 50/92)"
    },
    "principle": "Hold the MEANING of each threshold constant across proteins, not its value. Every factor is derived from a measured baseline or a geometric ratio, not fitted to make a gate pass.",
    "unchanged": "Environment code, policy schema, verifier, reward form - all frozen at Abeta42.",
    "general_finding": "Every damage channel that SUMS over beads or pairs is extensive: pathology (core-pair mass), geometry (bonded-term count), and disrupted_structure (protective-pair mass). None of them port between proteins of different fragment size without normalisation."
  },
  "_polar_zipper": {
